   "html_text": "In evaluating Rédei’s argument it is important to ask what counts as a physical thing. Einstein mentioned two possible candidates: bodies and fields. Howard’s separability principle permits a natural transposition of Einstein’s real state separability principle to field theory. Entangled states in AQFT violate section 5’s state separability principle just as they do in nonrelativistic quantum mechanics even though the split property and related independence conditions on their algebras hold. So ",
